Do not hold a cdp session lock while looking a peer up for routing.

AAASendMessage() and AAASendRecvMessage() route a request with the
session of its Session-Id locked (cdp_get_session()), and routing looks
the peer up with get_peer_by_fqdn(), which takes peer_list_lock. Two other
paths take the same locks in the other order:

  check_application() (cdp_has_app())  peer_list_lock, then a peer's lock
  sm_process(Send_Message)             a peer's lock, then a session's,
                                       in Snd_Message()

so a request being routed, a cdp_has_app() and a request being sent to
that peer close a cycle. The S-CSCF of the load test hit it at about
70 calls/s: a CCR-T for a BYE held the OCS peer and waited for a session
slot, cdp_has_app() held peer_list_lock and waited for the OCS peer, and
three initial and interim CCRs held session slots and waited for
peer_list_lock. Every SIP worker, the cdp receiver and timer and the
xhttp /metrics then waited behind them; the process never recovered.

get_first_connected_route() already drops the session lock around the
sticky peer's lookup ("Don't attempt to hold two locks at same time").
Do the same around the loop over the routing entries, which does not
touch the session, and around the Destination-Host lookup in
get_routing_peer(). Callers still get the session back locked.

diff --git a/src/modules/cdp/routing.c b/src/modules/cdp/routing.c
index 24ffd98..1fc1674 100644
--- a/src/modules/cdp/routing.c
+++ b/src/modules/cdp/routing.c
@@ -110,6 +110,13 @@ peer *get_first_connected_route(
 		}
 	}
 
+	/* get_peer_by_fqdn() takes peer_list_lock, and check_application()
+	 * takes it before a peer's lock, while sm_process() takes a peer's lock
+	 * before a session's (Snd_Message()): holding the session lock across
+	 * it closes that cycle, and every SIP worker of a busy CSCF ends up
+	 * waiting in it. The loop does not touch the session. */
+	if(cdp_session)
+		AAASessionsUnlock(cdp_session->hash);
 	for(i = r; i; i = i->next) {
 		if(peer_count >= LB_MAX_PEERS)
 			break;
@@ -139,6 +146,9 @@ peer *get_first_connected_route(
 		}
 	}
 
+	if(cdp_session)
+		AAASessionsLock(cdp_session->hash);
+
 	if(peer_count == 0) {
 		return 0;
 	}
@@ -258,7 +268,12 @@ peer *get_routing_peer(cdp_session_t *cdp_session, AAAMessage *m)
 
 	if(destination_host.len) {
 		/* There is a destination host present in the message try and route directly there */
+		/* not under the session lock: see get_first_connected_route() */
+		if(cdp_session)
+			AAASessionsUnlock(cdp_session->hash);
 		p = get_peer_by_fqdn(&destination_host);
+		if(cdp_session)
+			AAASessionsLock(cdp_session->hash);
 		if(p && (p->state == I_Open || p->state == R_Open)
 				&& (peer_handles_application(p, app_id)
 						|| peer_handles_application(p, RELAY_APP_ID))) {
